    "result": "Done! I've created `src/order-agent.js` with the two required exports:\n\n**`getOrderStatus`** \u2014 An AI SDK tool that:\n- Takes `{ orderId }` as input\n- Receives the current customer ID through AI SDK 7's per-tool context (`{ customerId }`), not as closure or model input\n- Returns `{ orderId, status, eta }` if the order belongs to the customer\n- Returns `{ orderId, error: 'not found' }` if the order doesn't exist or doesn't belong to the customer\n\n**`answerOrderQuestion(model, question, { customerId })`** \u2014 An agent function that:\n- Uses `generateText` with the `getOrderStatus` tool to answer customer questions\n- Gives the model the system instruction: \"You are Acme's order-status assistant. Answer in one short sentence.\"\n- Limits the model to 5 steps maximum using `stepCountIs(5)`\n- Returns `{ answer, lookedUp, inputTokens, outputTokens }` with the model's response, order IDs looked up, and token counts\n\nThe implementation has been tested and verified to work with multiple scenarios including customer isolation, token accumulation, and direct answers without tool calls.",
